        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-18T22:41:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hm, so we\u0027re really sure there\u0027s no form of the EC codebase that might want less precision? I was hoping to keep this change mostly to be a refactoring, and (try to) not let larger feature-level decisions creep in. My vote would be to keep it the way I have it for now, and then later we can look at the value of CONFIG_CONSOLE_VERBOSE and remove it as a separate change. Is there a reason I\u0027m missing why an additional subroutine is bad?",
      "parentUuid": "2bb674ca_19955c56",
      "range": {
